1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,207
Day 58: OpenSRE, a self-hosted agent that investigates CI

2
00:00:05,207 --> 00:00:09,044
failures, tested without any paid API key.

3
00:00:09,494 --> 00:00:11,520
OpenSRE reads failing CI logs,

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:15,370
figures out whether the pipeline or the code is at fault,

5
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:18,341
and can push a fix back to the pull request.

6
00:00:18,791 --> 00:00:23,150
Before anything else, OpenSRE validates the configured LLM

7
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:23,826
provider.

8
00:00:23,826 --> 00:00:27,057
With nothing set, it defaults to Anthropic.

9
00:00:27,507 --> 00:00:31,177
Once validated, it builds a LangGraph state machine and

10
00:00:31,177 --> 00:00:33,846
gathers evidence in a plan actions node.

11
00:00:34,296 --> 00:00:37,808
That node asks an LLM client what to check next.

12
00:00:37,808 --> 00:00:42,271
It can route to a local Ollama server instead of a cloud API,

13
00:00:42,271 --> 00:00:44,246
so no paid key is required.

14
00:00:44,696 --> 00:00:48,563
With no provider set, OpenSRE crashed on a raw Python

15
00:00:48,563 --> 00:00:52,285
traceback, since it silently defaults to Anthropic.

16
00:00:52,285 --> 00:00:55,350
Setting one variable, LLM_PROVIDER=ollama,

17
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:59,874
let it reach the real LangGraph pipeline before failing on the

18
00:00:59,874 --> 00:01:00,822
network call.

19
00:01:01,272 --> 00:01:03,241
Apache-2.0, self-hosted.

20
00:01:03,241 --> 00:01:08,082
Full write-up, sources and the Ollama follow-up on Zenn and

21
00:01:08,082 --> 00:01:08,656
GitHub.
